<section class="ihero"><div class="ihero-text"><div class="ihero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span><a href="/appraisal-practice/">Services</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span><span aria-current="page">Neutral Umpire Services</span></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Neutral Insurance Umpire Services in Alaska</h1><p class="lede">When two appraisers cannot agree, the umpire decides the items in dispute. We serve as a neutral umpire on panels where we have no prior role and no relationship with either side.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn line light" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="facts"><div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Impartial third member</dd></div><div><dt>Appointed by</dt><dd>Both appraisers or a court</dd></div><div><dt>Decides</dt><dd>Disputed items only</dd></div></dl></div></div><figure class="ihero-photo"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation-laptop.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-laptop-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation-laptop.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:900px) 100vw, 55vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></figure></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>The umpire's role</h2>
<p>Under a typical appraisal clause, the two appraisers choose an umpire. If they cannot agree on one, either side may ask a court to appoint one. The umpire's job is to resolve the specific items the appraisers could not agree on. An award signed by the umpire and either appraiser sets the amount of loss.</p>
<h2>How we work as an umpire</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Disclosure first.</strong> Before accepting, we disclose any prior contact with the parties, appraisers or property.</li>
<li><strong>Clear ground rules.</strong> We set out how submissions, site visits and communications will work, so both sides are treated equally.</li>
<li><strong>Focus on the disputed items.</strong> We review what the appraisers have already agreed and concentrate on what remains.</li>
<li><strong>Written, itemized award.</strong> The award states the amount for each disputed item, separating replacement cost and actual cash value where needed.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Who uses umpire services</h2>
<p>Appraisers representing policyholders, appraisers representing carriers, and courts appointing umpires. We accept umpire appointments only on claims where we have had no other role.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Umpire versus appraiser</b>We never serve as an umpire on a claim where we acted as an appraiser or reviewed the estimate for either side.</div>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who pays the umpire?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Most appraisal clauses split the umpire's fee equally between the policyholder and the insurer. Check your policy.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can the umpire decide coverage?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Generally no. The umpire resolves differences on the amount of loss for the items submitted.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if the appraisers cannot agree on an umpire?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many policies allow either party to ask a court in the state where the property is located to appoint one.</p></div></details></div><h2>Related services</h2><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel" href="/appraisal-practice/appraisal-panel-representation/"><small>Service</small><span>Appraisal Panel Representation</span><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/appraisal-practice/home-insurance-claim-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Homeowner Claim Appraisal</span><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/appraisal-practice/commercial-hoa-condo-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Commercial, HOA &amp; Condo Appraisal</span><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><aside class="side"><div class="side-stick"><div class="side-box call"><h2 class="side-h">Talk it through</h2><p>Free first con